## Never use

- jQuery, Bootstrap, Material UI, plain CSS files
- Express directly (use Hono if not Next.js)
- Raw SQL strings concatenated with user input
- localStorage for anything sensitive
- `any` in TypeScript without an inline justifying comment
- Direct AI API calls (always route through classifier — see AI routing pattern)

## Always do

- `pnpm typecheck && pnpm test` before opening a PR
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`
- Branch naming: `<type>/<short-description>`
- Tests for any function touching money, auth, or data deletion
- Zod 4 schemas for all external inputs
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed
- API routes only when server-only secrets needed; otherwise Server Actions
- All env vars typed (t3-env or equivalent)
- Search before you grep: if the project has a `.leann/` index, answer where/how questions with one LEANN MCP search first; grep only for exact strings
- Before building a new module, run the reuse check (`/plan-feature` does it automatically); after building something reusable, `/extract-pattern`

