## When to use what

| Situation | Reach for |
| :-- | :-- |
| Quick, single-context task | Just do it in the main thread |
| A side task that would flood context (search, logs, one file's analysis) | A **subagent** (`.claude/agents/`) |
| A repeated checklist / procedure you paste often | A **slash command** (`.claude/commands/`) |
| A job needing many agents, branching, or cross-checking (deep review, audit, migration, multi-angle design) | A **saved Workflow recipe** (`.claude/workflows/`) |

## Dynamic Workflows — house policy

Saved `Workflow()` recipes live in `.claude/workflows/` and auto-register as `/<name>`. The kit ships
seven: `exhaustive-review`, `codebase-map`, `security-sweep`, `design-panel`, `safe-migration`,
`release-readiness`, `fast-dag-build`.

- **Two profiles, default Best.** Every recipe reads `args.mode` (`best` default / `saver`). `best` =
  max quality+speed (wide fan-out, 5 Sonnet skeptics/finding, Opus synthesis); `saver` = token-optimised
  (narrow fan-out, Haiku skeptics, Sonnet synthesis). Switch with `/mode best|saver`. On Max plans token
  cost isn't the constraint — the **weekly Opus cap** is — so even Best keeps bulk leaves (skeptics,
  grind) on Sonnet/Haiku to preserve it.
- **Opt-in & costly.** Workflows run only on the word "workflow", `/effort ultracode`, or running a
  saved recipe, and cost meaningfully more tokens than a normal turn — scope first.
- **Authoring rule.** `export const meta = {…}` must be a pure literal; recipes are plain JS with **no
  filesystem/shell/env access** (all config via `args`). See `.claude/workflows/README.md`.

